  {
    "skills": "add-subtract-or-multiply-fractions",
    "question_text": "Multiply. Write your answer as a fraction or as a whole or mixed number. $5 \\times \\frac{7}{9}$=_",
    "tag": "Gr6_10_E1",
    "question_number": "1_3",
    "question_type": "Fractions Fill in the blank",
    "correct_answers": [
      [
        "3",
        "8",
        "9"
      ]
    ],
    "solution": [
      [
        "1/2",
        "First, write 5 as a fraction: $5 = \\frac{5}{1}$"
      ],
      [
        "2/2",
        "Now multiply the numerators and the denominators: $\\frac{5}{1} \\times \\frac{7}{9} = \\frac{5 \\times 7}{1 \\times 9} = \\frac{35}{9}$"
      ],
      [
        "3/3",
        "Write $\\frac{35}{9}$ as a mixed number. Divide 35 by 9 = 3 remainder 8, so: $\\frac{35}{9} = 3\\frac{8}{9}$"
      ]
    ],
    "has_alternate_answers": false
  },
  {
    "skills": "add-subtract-or-multiply-fractions",
    "question_text": "Add. $\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}$ = Do not need to simplify.=_",
    "tag": "Gr6_10_E1",
    "question_number": "1_2",
    "question_type": "Fractions Fill in the blank",
    "correct_answers": [
      [
        "1",
        "2",
        "4"
      ],
      [
        "1",
        "1",
        "2"
      ],
      [
        "",
        "6",
        "4"
      ],
      [
        "",
        "3",
        "2"
      ]
    ],
    "solution": [
      [
        "1/3",
        "Both fractions already have the same denominator. So just add the numerators: $\\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{6}{4}$"
      ],
      [
        "2/3",
        "You can also write the answer as a mixed number. First divide: $6 \\div 4 = 1$ with 2 left over"
      ],
      [
        "3/3",
        "Now rewrite the answer: $\\frac{6}{4} = 1\\frac{2}{4}$. You do not have to simplify, but it can be simplified to $1\\frac{1}{2}$"
      ]
    ],
    "has_alternate_answers": true
  },
  {
    "skills": "add-subtract-or-multiply-fractions",
    "question_text": "Subtract. $\\frac{7}{10}-\\frac{1}{2}$ = Do not need to simplify.=_",
    "tag": "Gr6_10_E1",
    "question_number": "1_1",
    "question_type": "Fill in the blank",
    "correct_answers": [
      [
        "2/10"
      ],
      [
        "1/5"
      ]
    ],
    "solution": [
      [
        "1/3",
        "You can use 10 as the common denominator."
      ],
      [
        "2/3",
        "With 10 as the common denominator, we need the fraction $\\frac{1}{2}$ to have a denominator of 10. So multiply the numerator and denominator by 5 to find an equivalent fraction. $\\frac{1 \\times 5}{2 \\times 5} = \\frac{5}{10}$"
      ],
      [
        "3/3",
        "Now subtract the fractions. Subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. $\\frac{7}{10} - \\frac{5}{10} = \\frac{2}{10}$. You do not have to simplify, but it can be simplified to $\\frac{1}{5}$"
      ]
    ],
    "has_alternate_answers": true
  },
